  "place": "drifts over a capped fumarole east of Stiltreach at dusk; the stilt folk say it was the well-keeper",
  "_doc": "Expansion 1 (Vharlen). The well-keeper of an old stilt village, now a wisp of fumarole steam. He breathes scalding mist in a cone and pulls the mud out from under a player (it roots them). At half health he lets the fumarole go: three ripples of steam roll outward one after the other (step through each as it passes), and the ground sucks at every player.",
  "party": {
    "solo": "Fair solo at 15; time the ripples.",
    "small": "Right for 2-3.",
    "full": "Easy.",
    "m5": "M5 adds health per extra player and one more copy of the spread/scatter shapes for parties of 4-5; mechanics stay the same."
  },
  "hpMult": 2,
  "arena": {
    "radius": 24
  },
  "say": {
    "pull": [
      "The steam over the vent takes the shape of an old man with a bucket.",
      "'Who's been drawing from my well?'"
    ],
    "death": "Old Wellen thins into plain steam. The vent goes quiet.",
    "reset": "Old Wellen settles back over his vent."
  },
